      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We need to calculate the average number of rounds played by each golfer. First, we're given the number of golfers who took $1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 rounds of golf. There are $1$ golfer who took $1$ round, $2$ golfers who took $2$ rounds, $2$ golfers who took $3$ rounds, $3$ golfers who took $4$ rounds, and $5$ golfers who took $5$ rounds.\n\nWe need a formula to calculate the average, which will be total rounds played divided by the total number of golfers. We can multiply the total number of golfers by the number of rounds they played.\n\nWe calculate the total number of golfers:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n&1 \\text{ golfer who took 1 round of golf} + 2 \\text{ golfers who took 2 rounds of golf} + 2 \\text { golfers who took 3 rounds} \\\\\n&+ 3 \\text{ golfers who took 4 rounds} + 5 \\text{ golfers who took 5 rounds} \\\\\n&= 1 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 5 \\\\\n&= 13 \\text{ golfers}\n\\end{align*} We then multiply the total number of golfers by the number of rounds each golfer played to find the total number of rounds.\n\n\\begin{align*}\n&1 \\text{ golfer who took 1 round of golf} \\times 1 \\\\\n&+ 2 \\text{ golfers who took 2 rounds of golf} \\times 2 \\\\\n&+ 2 \\text{ golfers who took 3 rounds of golf} \\times 3 \\\\\n&+ 3 \\text{ golfers who took 4 rounds of golf} \\times 4 \\\\\n&+ 5 \\text{ golfers who took 5 rounds of golf} \\times 5 \\\\\n&= 1 \\times 1 + 2 \\times 2 + 2 \\times 3 +3 \\times 4 + 5 \\times 5 \\\\\n&= 1 + 4 + 6 + 12 + 25 \\\\\n&= 48 \\text{ rounds}\n\\end{align*} We divide 48 by the numbers of rounds to find the average.\n\n\\begin{align*}\n&\\dfrac{\\text{total number of rounds}} {\\text{total number of golfers}} =  \\dfrac {48}{13}\\approx 3.6923\\\n\\end{align*} Rounded to the nearest whole number, the answer is $\\boxed{4}.$.",
